V0-4 01 Mar 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos004 - Post focal-place version 4 software.  Used for testing the GMOS
system during March 2000 (device layer only). Uses November 1999 version of the
HIA records.  ARCHIVED.

V0-5 10 Mar 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos005 - Post focal-plane version 5 software.  Newest version which uses the
February 2000 version of the HIA records. This version has a much more reliable
assembly layer.  ARCHIVED.

V0-6 10 Apr 2000 SMB:
---------------------
The result of the first attempt to integrate the pre and post focal-plane
software. This version uses unchanged device record but required several OMS
scan tasks. Saved on 10 April 2000.  ARCHIVED.

V0-7 15 Apr 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos007 - First fully integrated pre and post focal-plane software. This
resulted from William Rambold's visit of April 2000.  The device control record
has been modified to satisfy both pre and post focal-plane requirements. There
are currently four versions available: A full version for the real hardware,
databases with simulated post or pre focal-plane hardware, and a fully
simulated database. Saved 15 April 2000.  ARCHIVED.

V0-8 01 Jun 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos008 - Version containing commented code from William Rambold with serious
memory corruption problems. Use of this version is not recommended. Saved in
June 2000.  ARCHIVED.

V0-9 12 Jul 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos009 - Version with the memory corruption problems contained in gmos008
fixed. Saved 12 July 2000.  ARCHIVED.

V1-0 31 Jul 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos010 - This is the first version of the software to use the new turret
microswitches, rather than prompting the user to index the turret on the lower
hard limit. Saved 31 July 2000. ARCHIVED.

V1-1 16 Aug 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos011 - The first version of the software to make use of the Instrument
Sequencer. This version of the software was used during the first GMOS cold
tests from 18-31 August 2000.  This software automatically switches off the
mask opto sensors, but requires that the sensors be switched on manually before
operating the mask assembly. Saved 16 August 2000.  ARCHIVED.

V1-2 29 Sep 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos012 - This version of the software fixes the mask assembly opto sensor
problem and has the ability to park the filter assembly at various load
positions. It also fixes some minor bugs noticed during and after the cold
tests and fixes several bugs detected during the Instrument Sequencer tests.
Used extensively for grating tilt repeatability tests.  Saved 29 September
2000. ARCHIVED

V1-3 13 Oct 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos013 - This version contains the changes to the device record which had to
be made to support the new wavefront sensor. From this version of the software
onwards, lookup tables are obtained from the /gemini/gmos directory. Saved 13
October 2000. ARCHIVED.

V1-4 01 Nov 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos014 - This version contains Bob Wooff's October 2000 release of the
wavefront sensor software. It also contains some bug fixes to the filter and
grating software. Saved 1 November 2000. ARCHIVED

V1-5 17 Nov 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos015 - This version fixes problems found in the OIWFS to TCS interface and
corrects bugs found in the flexure control part of the GMOS Instrument
Sequencer. It also contains some bug fixes to the device and assembly records.
This version was used for the first set of flexure tests. Saved 17 November
2000. ARCHIVED

V1-6 12 Dec 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos016 - This version fixes problems found during the first set of flexure
tests. It also "jiggles" the grating tilt drives automatically and leaves them
out of contact with the worm, to give better repeatability.  This version was
used for the second set of flexure tests. This version includes a 7 second
delay before lowering the turret. Saved 12 December 2000. ARCHIVED

V1-7 01 Feb 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos017 - This version has better handling of barcode read failures by the mask
and filter assemblies. It also has some major changes to the instrument
sequencer, in which the focus offset of a filter is separated into its
wavelength and surface curvature components, and a grating may have a surface
curvature components. The effective wavelength of an observation is derived
from the filter in imaging mode and from the grating settings in spectroscopy
mode.  This change requires a change in format of the "filters.lut" and
"gratings.lut" files.  Several improvements have also been made to the
reliability and maintainability of the instrument sequencer code and
readability of the dm screens. Saved 1 February 2001.

V1-8 13 Feb 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos018 - This version includes all the changes Bob Wooff made to use the
new interlock hardware. Older versions of the software will not work with
the new hardware. Saved 13 February 2001.

V1-9 20 Feb 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos019 - This version contains all the changes made to the flexure control
software which converts TCS coordinates to GMOS coordinates and converts those
GMOS coordinates into a flexure offset using a model based on actual GMOS
flexure measurements. Saved 20 February 2001.

V2-0 26 Feb 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos020 - This version allows masks to be selected by name as well as by
barcode ID. It also extends the acceptable wavelength range to 1100nm, The mask
and OIWFS assemblies are converted to use the same error reporting scheme as
the post focal plane assemblies.  Saved 26 February 2001.

V2-1 02 Mar 2000 SMB:
---------------------
gmos021 - This version fixes a problem selecting the same mask twice in the
mask assembly and corrects a bug in the instrument sequencer debug command. A
problem with the messages displayed by the new interlock software has been
fixed.  The assembly and device record code also display error messages on the
console by default. Some bad practise with "void *" pointers in the instrument
sequencer code tidied up.  Used for GMOS science tests. Saved 2 March 2001.

V2-2 08 Mar 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos022 - This version fixes a bug found in the OIWFS SAD and changes the way
the system health is determined to more closely match Gemini requirements.
There are minor changes to some of the "dm" screens. This frozen version will
be used for GMOS acceptance tests and for post shipping evaluation. Saved 8
March 2001.
FIRST VERSION SAVED TO CVS REPOSITORY AT GEMINI HBF - gmoscc and gmosis merged.

V2-2-1 16 Apr 2001 SMB:
-----------------------
This version is identical to V2-2 except additional housekeeping changes
were made to allow the software work properly at HBF:
- Top level gmosIocAnnex and sim2 scripts were added, for VME crates
  contacted through an annex.
- The lookup tables directory was changed from /home/smb/gmos/lut
  back to /gemini/gmos/lut.
- dm screen colours were changed to match the descriptions in the
  "GMOS Software User Manual".
- Startup scripts were edited to refer to "$(iocpath)" rather than
  "$(version)" or "$(install)".

V2-2-2 16 Apr 2001 SMB:
-----------------------
This version is identical to V2-2-1 except the shell scripts have been
moved to the bin/solaris directory and the PATH and EPICS_DISPLAY_PATH
variables have been defined to include /gemini/gmos/gmos/bin and
/gemini/gmos/gmos/data.

V2-2-3 20 Apr 2001 SMB:
-----------------------
This version is identical to V2-2-2 except that the wait time associated
with the grating lifter has been increased to compensate for the denser
air in Hilo as compared with Edinburgh. The error messages reported by
some of the mask checkout scripts have been made more explicit.

V2-2-4 23 Apr 2001 SMB:
-----------------------
This version is identical to V2-2-3 except that a smoothing factor has been
applied to the mask LVDT readings to cope with increased noise in the mask LVDT
electronics. A gmosannex script has been added because the connections made by
the gmos and gmosdc scripts to the annex have a problem with multiple carriage
returns.

V2-3 23 Apr 2001 SMB:
---------------------
gmos023 - This version, which has been merged with V2-2-4, contains fixes to
the following problems:
- #168 spontaneous motion error: OIWFS devices will no longer time out
  after being moved manually by a significant amount.
- #196 DEBUG macro cannot display floating point values: All DEBUG macros
  now use printf and can display floating point values.
- #218 Device control HSWA field can stick: A field monitoring problem
  that may have caused this bug has been identified and fixed. The result
  still needs to be tested.
- #258 Device control record does not fully simulate: A problem that
  caused the simulation mode to be set up incorrectly if the mode
  is changed after the device has already executed an INIT has been fixed.
THIS IS THE VERSION USED FOR THE SOFTWARE ACCEPTANCE TESTS ON 12 APRIL 2001.

V2-4 30 Apr 2001 SMB:
---------------------
This version fixes problems seen during the software acceptance tests:
- The filter and grating assemblies forward the TEST command to their
  devices.
- The instrument sequencer includes the dtaXoffset, dtaYoffset and dtaZoffset
  records and keeps them up to date with the translation stage base
  position.
- The instrument sequencer updates the dtaZstart, dtaZend and dtaZmean
  records each time an observation is made.
- Translation assembly test script enhanced to include a check on the
  actual position arriving to within a small tolerance of the target
  position.
In addition:
- Mask extractor ID position adjusted to read barcodes on masks rather
  than mask frames.
- gmosHelp and gmosTest commands added, with online help.
- The endObserve command clears the detector controller observe CAD
  record, as an attempt to work around a channel access problem.
- Test script log files are now written to a separate directory for
  each date.
- A gmSeqTopMKRRtc1 version of the EPICS database created to connect
  to the TCS simulator, and a corresponding startupTc1 script created.
- Startup scripts modified to generate labels using the standard instrument
  name, which is GMOS-N.
THIS IS THE VERSION USED TO TEST THE TRANSLATION STAGE ON 02 MAY 2001.

V2-5 15 May 2001 SMB:
---------------------
This version is the same as V2-4 with
- All references to HSWA field removed from checkout scripts,
  since that field is not important and does not always accurately
  reflect the state of the hardware (problem 218).
- Some cosmetic improvements to the "dm" screens. (Many of the font
  sizes were much larger on Hilo workstations, rendering some text
  information unreadable). Interlock information on the top level
  WFS screen corrected.
- Bob Wooff and Malcolm Smith's changes to the OIWFS focus settings.
  The OIWFS will now return a focus offset based on the different
  between the probe's position and the telescope focal surface rather
  than the flat mask plane. The software has also been given the ability
  to change the focal surface when the AtmDC is fitted, but this part
  of the code is will be tested later.
- More on-line help.
THIS IS THE VERSION RICK USED TO CHECK THE OIWFS FOCUS OFFSETS ON 15 MAY
2001

V2-6 17 May 2001 SMB:
-------------------------
This version is the same as V2-5 with
- GMOS sequencer startup changed so the detector controller apply record
  is not activated during a reboot.
- gmOiwfsCalibrate.c function modified so it will build correctly.
- Malcolm Smith's bug fix to CalcApproxProbePosition in gmOiwfsCalc.c.

V2-7 ?? May 2001 ???
--------------------
A future version will contain Malcolm Smith's ADC correction code.
